{
  "description": "Lag(n=2, length=2): a unit is two consecutive responses read as their operanda; units do not overlap. A unit is reinforced at its second response iff it differs from each of the previous two units (fewer while fewer exist). Units LL (first, reinforced), LR (reinforced), LL (equals the unit two back, no), RR (reinforced), LL (equals the unreinforced LL two units back, no). The unreinforced LL still enters the comparison list. A tick changes nothing; the first response of a unit never reinforces.",
